{
  "case_id": "2020-19-511",
  "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Facebook, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The TCPA defines an Automatic Telephone Dialing System as equipment with the capacity to store or produce telephone numbers to be called, using a random or sequential number generator, and to dial such number."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The TCPA defines an Automatic Telephone Dialing System as equipment with the capacity to store or produce telephone numbers to be called, using a random or sequential number generator, and to dial such number."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Washington Legal Foundation",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there is an amicus brief by the Washington Legal Foundation that addresses this issue specifically, and what they point out is that in more recent statutes, when Congress is -- when Congress addresses calls and texts, they do so either conjunctively or disjunctively."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you think it would have some utility -- I mean, I -- I guess what I'm getting at here is I'm wondering"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the ATDS provisions were addressed to something broader than random or sequential dialing, Congress's decision to leave the residential landlines unprotected would be inexplicable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I have two questions. The first is the one that I asked Mr. Clement: does it make any sense to talk about a system that uses a --a random or sequential number generator in the very process of storing telephone numbers?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "could a TCPA lawsuit against individual smartphone users actually prevail, given that smartphones don't automatically dial phone numbers in the ways of this -- in the way that a sequential numbering system does?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So doesn't that suggest that your definition is wrong? I mean, would Congress really have wanted to depart from all of those state statutes in this particular way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My -- my question is, does it make any difference in the real world?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And that part of the statute still makes sense and applies today, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, can I stop you right there? Do you think -- and this gets to Justice Kagan's question, what Congress was drawing on -- do you think they meant \"and\" instead of \"or\" and made a mistake?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, if we rule your way, the logical consequence is that every cell phone owner would be subject to the harsh criminal and civil penalties of the CPA. Could you give me a reason, other than that it hasn't happened yet, for -- for why Congress would have intended that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I think you're going to have to answer me more clearly than that. You don't think that cell phone users will do what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: You -- you conceded that the grammar here is awkward, but I'd like to pick up where Justice Kagan left off. And -- and I -- I think you -- you have -- certainly have an argument that grammar doesn't exhaust meaning, fine. But on what basis is this sentence grammatical?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, let me ask you this. In -- in response to Justice Alito, you were talking about what happens if --if we were to interpret the statute your way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Congress can define anything to mean anything it wishes, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13fce8305df8d3b3abd89915d46d7509034e7ad80e1d54b57e911e00ad58dff9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13fce8305df8-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you,\ncounsel. The case is submitted."
    },
